      "kind": "nav",
      "description": "Selected destinations use a soft seafoam fill and a persistent text label.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-portal-nav\" aria-label=\"Portal preview\"><a href=\"#learn\" aria-current=\"page\">Learning portal</a><a href=\"#paths\">Learning paths</a><a href=\"#progress\">Your progress</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-portal-nav{display:grid;gap:6px;padding:16px;width:224px;background:#141a1c;font:13px/1.6 \"Manrope\",\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-portal-nav a{display:flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;padding:10px 12px;border-radius:6px;color:var(--muted,#a5afad);text-decoration:none;transition:background 150ms,color 150ms}.ds-portal-nav a:hover{background:var(--raised,#1e2629);color:var(--text,#eceee9)}.ds-portal-nav a[aria-current=\"page\"]{background:var(--accent-soft,#22372d);color:var(--accent,#b6dac6);font-weight:650}.ds-portal-nav a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#b6dac6);outline-offset:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Public navigation",
      "kind": "nav",
      "description": "Horizontal public links use an underline for the current destination.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-public-nav\" aria-label=\"Public preview\"><a href=\"#home\" aria-current=\"page\">Home</a><a href=\"#about\">About</a></nav>",
      "css": ".ds-public-nav{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:28px;padding:12px;background:var(--bg,#101416);font:13px/1.6 \"Manrope\",\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-public-nav a{padding-block:12px;color:var(--muted,#a5afad);text-decoration:none;text-underline-offset:5px}.ds-public-nav a:hover,.ds-public-nav a[aria-current=\"page\"]{color:var(--text,#eceee9)}.ds-public-nav a[aria-current=\"page\"]{text-decoration:underline}.ds-public-nav a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#b6dac6);outline-offset:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Topic label",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "topic-label",
      "description": "Passive mathematics metadata keeps its category color contained.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-topic\">Foundations</span>",
      "css": ".ds-topic{display:inline-flex;padding:3px 7px;border-radius:4px;background:var(--topic-math-surface,#21332c);color:var(--topic-math,#a7ceba);font:11px/1.6 \"Manrope\",\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Next lesson panel",
      "kind": "card",
      "description": "The dashboard gives its next lesson a contained green surface.",
      "html": "<article class=\"ds-next\"><h2>Up next</h2><h3>Build your foundations</h3><p>Continue with your next lesson in the learning portal.</p><a href=\"#lesson\">Open lesson →</a></article>",
      "css": ".ds-next{padding:26px;border:1px solid #3a5045;border-radius:12px;background:#1b2a25;color:var(--text,#eceee9);font:14px/1.6 \"Manrope\",\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif}.ds-next h2{margin:0 0 20px;color:#b5c9bc;font-size:13px;font-weight:600}.ds-next h3{margin:0;max-width:28ch;font-size:25px;line-height:1.35;letter-spacing:-.025em;font-weight:600}.ds-next p{margin:12px 0 24px;max-width:65ch;color:#b6c3bb;font-size:13px;line-height:1.8}.ds-next a{display:inline-flex;min-height:42px;align-items:center;padding:11px 17px;border-radius:7px;background:var(--accent,#b6dac6);color:var(--accent-ink,#13241b);font-size:12px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none}.ds-next a:hover{background:var(--accent-hover,#cce8d9)}.ds-next a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#b6dac6);outline-offset:4px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Account feedback",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "Explicit wording accompanies status color, and errors receive keyboard focus.",
      "html": "<p class=\"ds-notice\" role=\"status\">A verification email has been requested. Check your inbox and spam folder.</p>",
      "css": ".ds-notice{padding:14px 16px;margin:24px 0 16px;border:1px solid var(--border,#303b3f);border-radius:6px;background:var(--accent-soft,#22372d);color:var(--success,#91d5a8);font:13px/1.8 \"Manrope\",\"Segoe UI\",system-ui,sans-serif;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.ds-notice:focus{outline:2px solid currentColor;outline-offset:3px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "A clear practice workbench",
    "overview": "A clear practice workbench. Charcoal grounds, warm off-white type, and restrained seafoam actions support reading, experimentation, and code. This records the implemented dark system on 7 November 2026 and supersedes the earlier light-theme notes, following the user's explicit direction.\n\nThe public introduction and learning portal share typography, color, and the compact ZeroShot mark. Their navigation and density stay distinct: broad public compositions explain the product; the portal puts the next task, saved work, and tools within reach. Component boundaries use tone and thin lines. Images of fictional users, decorative dashboards, and unsupported claims have no role in this system.\n\nImplementation sources are the global, marketing, portal, and authentication stylesheets, their current components, and the desktop/mobile review captures. This is a visual specification, not a release or accessibility certification.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Charcoal grounds, warm off-white type, and restrained seafoam actions.",
      "Shared typography and identity with separate public and learning navigation.",
      "Flat surfaces, thin borders, readable lesson rows, and explicit status text.",
      "Self-hosted Manrope for the interface and monospace for code."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Explicit State Rule",
        "body": "Pair every diagnostic color with meaningful text or an icon. Accent indicates interaction; it does not imply that a lesson has passed.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Separate Destinations Rule",
        "body": "The public home explains ZeroShot and links into `/learn/`; it does not impersonate the learner's personal dashboard. Keep return links visible in both environments.",
        "section": "layout"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do preserve the dark palette and distinguish the public website from the learning portal.",
      "Do use real interactive examples and actual learner state where available.",
      "Do keep focus visible, input labels explicit, and touch actions reachable.",
      "Do preserve guest learning and accurate local-storage explanations.",
      "Do keep code, content, and navigation in a readable order on narrow screens."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't reintroduce the rejected light theme or merge the public home into the dashboard.",
      "Don't fabricate learners, outcomes, testimonials, or synchronization capabilities.",
      "Don't use color alone to explain success, error, topic, or selection.",
      "Don't add decorative gradients, glow, or shadow-heavy containers to this flat system."
    ]
  }
}
